Z||000006||TheFiero64||02-28-2001||05:37 PM||||Directly from the link I posted<P>Red Line MTL may be used in transmissions which recommend 5W/10W30 motor oils.<P>The reason that many manufacturers have made recommendations of motor oils or ATFs is that <B>petroleum 80W gear oils</B> frequently do not shift well at low temperatures. Motor Oil has almost no extreme-pressure protection. In addition, multigrade motor oils and ATFs have very poor shear stability. <P>This fluid protects the transmission a lot better than engine oil. It also gives smoother shifting. I would recommend everyone to read the whole article. It was very informative.<P><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||TheFiero64||02-28-2001||05:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Will:<BR><B>What trans are you talking about?<P>The getrag has a dipstick close to the VSS.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I was talking about the Isuzu. I forgot the getrag has the dip-stick.<P>Thanks for reminding me. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
